  data: {
    LLM: 'The Jack and Nine of trumps are the most powerful cards (34 points together). If you have these, you have strong control of the trump suit. Always try to establish how many trumps your partner holds.\n\nRoem (melds) can significantly affect the score. A run of 3 (20 points) or 4 (50 points) can swing a hand. Be careful not to give opponents the cards they need for their melds. The Stuk (trump King and Queen) is worth 20 points and should be protected.\n\nSignaling: Partners use legal signals to communicate hand strength. A high-low signal in a suit suggests an even number of cards; low-high suggests odd. Master the Amsterdam vs Rotterdam rules about when you must trumpâ€”this affects endgame play significantly.',
    Player: 'The Jack and Nine of trumps are the most powerful cards (34 points together). If you have these, you have strong control of the trump suit. Always try to establish how many trumps your partner holds.\n\nRoem (melds) can significantly affect the score. A run of 3 (20 points) or 4 (50 points) can swing a hand. Be careful not to give opponents the cards they need for their melds. The Stuk (trump King and Queen) is worth 20 points and should be protected.\n\nSignaling: Partners use legal signals to communicate hand strength. A high-low signal in a suit suggests an even number of cards; low-high suggests odd. Master the Amsterdam vs Rotterdam rules about when you must trumpâ€”this affects endgame play significantly.',
