    advanced: 'Signaling: Partners use legal signals to communicate hand strength. A high-low signal in a suit suggests an even number of cards; low-high suggests odd. Master the Amsterdam vs Rotterdam rules about when you must trumpâ€”this affects endgame play significantly.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Remember the two different card orders: trick-taking order (Jack, Nine high in trumps) vs meld sequence order (Ace high)',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'The last trick is worth 10 pointsâ€”plan accordingly',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'If you choose trumps, you need 82+ points to score; aim for at least 90 to be safe',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Four Jacks is worth 200 pointsâ€”nearly enough to win a hand by itself',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "In Amsterdam rules, you can 'throw off' when partner is winning; in Rotterdam, you must always trump if possible",
